### 1.2. User Message Shape

You can standardize the user message as:

```ts
type SpecModeUserMessage = {
  mode: "Spec";
  instruction: string;         // freeform user request, can be long
  existingSpec: Spec | null;   // full JSON of the current Spec, or null
  userMetadata?: {
    author?: string;           // optional, can be used for changelog.author
    timestamp?: string;        // optional, ISO 8601; if absent, model can use a placeholder
  };
};
```

Example payload (for your orchestrator, not for the model):

```json
{
  "mode": "Spec",
  "instruction": "Refine the user stories for onboarding and add performance SLAs. Keep existing goals but mark reporting as lower priority.",
  "existingSpec": { /* full Spec JSON here, or null */ },
  "userMetadata": {
    "author": "alice",
    "timestamp": "2026-06-11T14:15:00Z"
  }
}
```

You then pass to the model as a user message, e.g.:

```text
You are in Spec mode.

User instruction:
<instruction text here>

Existing Spec (JSON or null):
<existingSpec JSON here or the word null>

User metadata (optional, may be null):
<JSON or null>

Your task:
